# Market Game

> Monthly, hands-on business simulation programs for chambers of commerce
> in the United States and internationally. Local business owners run
> competing companies in one shared market. Paid by the chamber or by a
> sponsor such as a bank. Free 60-minute demo game.

Market Game is built on {{ site.game.name }}, a team business simulation
created by {{ site.author.name }}. The game itself is described at
{{ site.game.url }}.

## Format

Participants sit in the chamber's room; the host joins by video on a big
screen. A bank or sponsor representative can be certified to host in person.
Each game is played in one of three formats:

{% for key, f in F %}- {{ f.name }} — {{ f.who | lower }}; {{ f.months }} game months, {{ f.hours }} hours; suggested ticket {{ f.ticket | usd }} per team.
{% endfor %}
Tickets are sold by the chamber, and the money stays with the chamber.

## Packages

The price is the same whether the chamber or a sponsor pays.

- Demo game — free, 60 minutes online.
- Pilot — {{ P.pilot.price | usd }}, one game. Founding Chamber of a state (the first chamber in the state to sign up): {{ pricing.foundingPilot | usd }}.
- Signature Event — {{ P.signature.price | usd }}, one game with branding, sponsor package, certificates and a board report.
- Annual Program — {{ P.annual.price | usd }} a year, {{ P.annual.games }} games (one a month), {{ P.annual.perGame | usd }} per game, billed monthly.

Options: in-person host +{{ O.inPerson | usd }} per game plus travel;
Spanish-language game +{{ O.spanish | usd }}; Elite format +{{ O.elite | usd }};
extra game {{ O.extraGame | usd }}; certification of a sponsor's own host
{{ O.hostCertification | usd }} per person.

## Banks and sponsors

Banks sponsor games at chambers: the loan inside the game carries the bank's
name, the bank's certified representative can host, participants may opt in
to be contacted. {{ P.annual.price | usd }} per chamber a year;
{{ B.volumePrice | usd }} per chamber from {{ B.volumeFrom }} chambers.
Exclusive Banking Partner: from {{ B.exclusiveMetroFrom }} chambers in a metro area
or {{ B.exclusiveStateFrom }} in a state. The activity may qualify for CRA
community development credit; the bank's CRA officer decides.

